{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.FullPoleStructureMassTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.FullPoleStructureMassTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.AbsoluteValue.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Monoid.Unbundled.Pow","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_truncation_bound_supercrit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_truncation_bound_supercrit","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L176-L192","doc":"**Supercritical truncation bound** (q > 1, the QOU substrate\nregime).  At `q₀ ≈ 1.110 > 1` the original `habiro_truncation_bound`\ndoes not apply directly — each new factor `|1 - q^{N+1}|` exceeds\n1.  Bridges via the Habiro `q ↔ q⁻¹` involution: `q > 1` implies\n`0 < q⁻¹ < 1`, so the original bound applies to `qPochhammer q⁻¹`.\n\nRef: [habiro2004] https://doi.org/10.2140/gt.2004.8.1127. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_truncation_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_truncation_bound","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L146-L174","doc":"**Habiro cyclotomic monotone bound** (purely structural).\n\nFor `0 < q < 1` and any truncation order `N`, the absolute\nPochhammer factor `|(q; q)_N|` is monotonically decreasing in\n`N`, since each new factor `(1 - q^{N+1})` lies in `(0, 1)`.\n\nScope: this lemma is stated for `q ∈ (0, 1)`. The QOU substrate\nsits at `q₀ ≈ 1.110 > 1`, so this bound does **not** apply\ndirectly at the substrate value: for `q > 1` the factor\n`|1 - q^{N+1}|` grows with `N` and `|(q;q)_N|` is monotone\n*increasing*. Truncation control at the substrate uses the\n`q ↔ q⁻¹` duality of the Hecke algebra (so that `q₀⁻¹ ≈ 0.901`\nfalls in the `(0, 1)` regime where this lemma applies); the\nduality bridge itself is left to `prop:full-pole-structure-mass-trace`\nin the narrative.\n\nRef: [habiro2004] https://doi.org/10.2140/gt.2004.8.1127. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.trivialOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.trivialOf","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L124-L144","doc":"**The class as stated constrains nothing** (added 2026-11-16).\n\nEvery polynomial `p` admits a `HabiroCompletion` with `trace = p`:\ntake `coeff 0 = p` and every other coefficient `0`. Then the\nresidual is `p` at `N = 0`, divisible by `(u;u)_0 = 1`, and `0` for\n`N ≥ 1`. So the docstring's \"non-vacuous\" reading is wrong: because\n`trace` is a free field and `coeff m` ranges over all of `ℤ[u]`, the\ndivisibility is always satisfiable. A contentful version would fix\n`trace` to the Markov trace of a given word and restrict the\ncoefficients (Habiro's theorem lives in the completion, where the\nexpansion is unique), which this file does not do. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.tail_in_ideal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.tail_in_ideal","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L119-L119","doc":"**Habiro-ideal property.**\n\nAt every truncation order `N`, the residual\n`trace - Σ_{m<N} a_m · (u;u)_m` lies in the principal ideal\n`((u;u)_N) ⊂ ℤ[u]`.\n\nNot a constraint as stated: `trace` and every `coeff m` are free,\nso `HabiroCompletion.trivialOf` satisfies it for any polynomial.\n(This read \"Non-vacuous\" until 2026-11-16.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.coeff","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L109-L109","doc":"Cyclotomic coefficients `a_m(T_w) ∈ ℤ[u]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.trace","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L107-L107","doc":"The Markov trace as a polynomial in `ℤ[u]` (Markov-normalised\nso that the result is integer-coefficient; the Laurent prefactor\n`D(u)` is folded into `trace`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroCompletion","kind":"class","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L62-L122","doc":"**Habiro completion of the Markov trace** (polynomial-ring form).\n\nThe mass trace of a closed braid `T_w` lies in the Habiro\nring `Ẑ[q]` and admits a unique cyclotomic expansion\n\n  tr_M(T_w, u) = Σ_{m ≥ 0} a_m(T_w) · (u; u)_m,\n  a_m(T_w) ∈ ℤ[u].\n\n(After Markov normalisation by `D(u)` — see field `trace`\nbelow — the prefactor leaves the cyclotomic coefficients\n`a_m` in the regular polynomial ring `ℤ[u]` rather than in\nthe Laurent ring `ℤ[u^±1]`.)\n\nThis class records the trace as a polynomial `trace : ℤ[u]`,\nthe cyclotomic coefficients `coeff : ℕ → ℤ[u]`, and the\nsubstantive axiom `tail_in_ideal`: at every truncation order\n`N`, the residual `trace - Σ_{m<N} a_m · (u;u)_m` lies in the\nHabiro ideal `((u;u)_N) ⊂ ℤ[u]`.\n\n**Why polynomial-typed.**  Polynomial divisibility by\n`qPochhammerPoly N` is non-trivial: the divisor has degree\n`N(N+1)/2` and is a non-unit, so the divisibility constraint\ncuts out a proper subset of polynomials.  An earlier\nℝ-evaluation-only formulation was vacuous (real divisibility by\na non-zero divisor is always solvable); the polynomial form\nabove repairs that and is what Gemini and Copilot reviews\nrequested as the \"honest Habiro-ideal\" statement.\n\n**ℝ-evaluation shadow.**  The earlier ℝ-evaluation observable\n(\"at any `q` annihilating `(q;q)_n`, the trace equals the\ncyclotomic partial sum up to order `n`\") follows by evaluating\nboth sides of `tail_in_ideal` at the relevant `q` (mapping\n`ℤ[u] → ℝ` via `Polynomial.eval₂ (Int.castRingHom ℝ) q`): if\n`(u;u)_N` divides the tail in `ℤ[u]`, then at any `q` where\n`(q;q)_N = 0` the tail evaluates to `0`.\n\nThe class is axiomatised: existence of the cyclotomic expansion\nfollows from Markov–Jones integrality plus sequential cyclotomic\ndivision, formalised in `cor:habiro-expansion-atomic`.\n\nRef: [habiro2004] https://doi.org/10.2140/gt.2004.8.1127. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:full-pole-structure-mass-trace","label":"prop:full-pole-structure-mass-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammerPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammerPoly","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L43-L60","doc":"**Polynomial q-Pochhammer** `(u; u)_m = Π_{k=1}^{m} (1 - u^k) ∈ ℤ[u]`.\n\nThis is the polynomial-ring companion of `qPochhammer` above.\n`qPochhammerPoly N` is a non-unit of degree `N(N+1)/2` in `ℤ[u]`,\nbut divisibility of the tail by it does not constrain a free\ncoefficient sequence: see `HabiroCompletion.trivialOf`.\n\nThe generic ring-valued analogue\n`QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer (u : R) : ℕ → R` over an arbitrary\n`[CommRing R]` lives in the sibling file\n`habiro-expansion-atomic.lean`; this is the specialisation\n`qPochhammer (Polynomial.X : Polynomial ℤ)`.  The two\ndefinitions are duplicated only because each sibling `.lean`\nfile is read standalone (not yet part of a shared Lake\nmodule); a future `QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroBasic` module would let\nboth files import a single source. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/full-pole-structure-mass-trace.lean#L37-L41","doc":"The real-valued q-Pochhammer factor\n`(q; q)_m = ∏_{k=1}^{m} (1 - q^k)`, used in the\n`0 < q < 1` truncation bound below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}